      "title": "Introduction",
      "scenes": [
        {
          "id": "c1-s1",
          "narration": "Welcome to our lesson on recursion! Today, we'll learn how recursion works using the factorial function.",
          "type": "title",
          "heading": "Recursion Explained",
          "subheading": "Understanding Recursion with Factorial"
        },
        {
          "id": "c1-s2",
          "narration": "Here's our function definition. We're defining a function named factorial that takes one parameter, n. The base case is when n equals zero, and the function returns one, stopping the recursion.",
          "type": "code",
          "code": "def factorial(n):\n    if n == 0:\n        return 1\n    return n * factorial(n - 1)\nprint(factorial(3))",
          "highlightLines": [
            1,
            2,
            3
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "c2",
      "title": "Recursive Call",
      "scenes": [
        {
          "id": "c2-s1",
          "narration": "If n is not zero, the function returns n multiplied by the factorial of n minus one. This is the recursive call.",
          "type": "code",
          "code": "def factorial(n):\n    if n == 0:\n        return 1\n    return n * factorial(n - 1)\nprint(factorial(3))",
          "highlightLines": [
            4
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "c2-s2",
          "narration": "Let's see how this works with an example. We start by calling factorial of three. Each call waits for the next one to finish.",
          "type": "diagram",
          "diagram": {
            "kind": "callstack",
            "frames": [
              {
                "call": "factorial(3)",
                "vars": {
                  "n": "3"
                }
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "c2-s3",
          "narration": "Next, factorial of two is called. It also waits for the next call to finish.",
          "type": "diagram",
          "diagram": {
            "kind": "callstack",
            "frames": [
              {
                "call": "factorial(3)",
                "vars": {
                  "n": "3"
                }
              },
              {
                "call": "factorial(2)",
                "vars": {
                  "n": "2"
                }
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "c2-s4",
          "narration": "Then, factorial of one is called. It waits for the next call to finish.",
          "type": "diagram",
          "diagram": {
            "kind": "callstack",
            "frames": [
              {
                "call": "factorial(3)",
                "vars": {
                  "n": "3"
                }
              },
              {
                "call": "factorial(2)",
                "vars": {
                  "n": "2"
                }
              },
              {
                "call": "factorial(1)",
                "vars": {
                  "n": "1"
                }
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "c2-s5",
          "narration": "Finally, factorial of zero is called. This is our base case, so it returns one.",
          "type": "diagram",
          "diagram": {
            "kind": "callstack",
            "frames": [
              {
                "call": "factorial(3)",
                "vars": {
                  "n": "3"
