    {
      "id": "c4",
      "title": "Recap",
      "scenes": [
        {
          "id": "c4-s1",
          "narration": "To wrap up, remember that recursion involves a function calling itself, always with a base case to stop it. Each call waits for the next one, and we compute the final result by combining the results of each call.",
          "type": "recap",
          "points": [
            "Recursion is a function calling itself.",
            "The base case stops the recursion.",
            "Each recursive call waits for the next one to finish.",
            "We compute the final result by multiplying the results of each call.",
            "In our example, factorial of three is six."
          ]
        }
      ]
